","source":["##Customer Analysis\n","\n","The customer analysis was conducted using the cleaned Online Retail dataset. Records with missing CustomerIDs and bad-debt adjustments were excluded from customer-level analysis.\n","\n","A total of 4,372 unique customers were identified. However, 135,037 transaction records had missing CustomerIDs, meaning some transactions could not be linked to individual customers.\n","\n","Key Findings\n","\n","1. Top customers: Customer 14646 generated the highest net revenue of 279,489.02 across 77 invoices. Customer 18102 followed with 256,438.49.\n","\n","2. Customer concentration: The top 10 customers generated 1,368,640.64, representing 16.53% of identified customer revenue.\n","\n","3. Purchasing frequency: Customer 14911 had the highest number of invoices (248), demonstrating that frequent purchasing does not necessarily translate into the highest revenue.\n","\n","4. Customer spending: Average revenue per customer was 1,893.53, while median revenue was 644.07. This suggests that a relatively small number of high-spending customers influence the average.\n","\n","5. Customer retention: Of the 4,372 identified customers, 3,059 (69.97%) made repeat purchases, while 1,313 (30.03%) made only one purchase.\n","\n","Business Recommendations\n","\n","- Develop customer retention strategies to encourage repeat purchases.\n","- Investigate the purchasing behaviour of high-value customers.\n","- Target one-time customers with promotions and follow-up marketing.\n","- Maintain accurate customer records to reduce missing CustomerIDs and improve customer analysis."],"metadata":{"id":"z1A9cqdYS2ri"}}]}